module

public import Rule30Open.Columns.ReachRefuted

/-!
# Entry into the only trap of period 6 is false

[WordTraps](WordTraps.md) checks `trap001011`, a trap of 29 cells for `001011`, the one block of period 6 with a trap,
and reduces the block to entry into it. In the game of 22 cells 28,666 of the 25,165,824 nodes can reach the trap cut
to 22 cells, and the white window at phase 0 is not among them. `back_trap001011` is that set of windows, checked closed
under predecessors, so by `not_absorption_back` of [ReachRefuted](ReachRefuted.md) the white right half driven by
`001011` from phase 0 never enters the trap, and the hypothesis of `not_eventually_001011_of_absorption` is false.

* `back_trap001011`, with `_check` and `_holds`: the windows of 22 cells that can reach the trap, by label.
* `trap001011_not_absorption_back`: entry into `trap001011` is false.

The tables come from `python -m computations.lock_chain --lean-six`. The natural-language argument is `SixRefuted.md`,
beside this file.
-/

@[expose] public section

-- Sequential elaboration: the kernel checks would otherwise run in parallel and stack their memory.
set_option Elab.async false

namespace Rule30Open

open Ruliology.CellularAutomata BitGame

/-- The windows of 22 cells from which the trap `trap001011` can be reached, by label: 28,666 of the 25,165,824 nodes of the game. -/
